  "question": {
    "text": "If the system of equations <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has a non-trivial solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "noyLG",
      "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
